# PRODUCTION database values, verbatim from deploy.ps1's main branch.
#
# ============================================================================
# WARNING — this points a container at the REAL Patroni production primary
# (192.168.0.162:6432). Using this file does NOT deploy to production —
# compose only starts containers on THIS machine; it has no equivalent to
# deploy.ps1's actual production rollout (scp+ssh to the Primary + DR
# servers, sudo systemctl restart, the production confirmation prompt).
# The only thing --env-file deploy/prod.env does is point a LOCAL container
# at the PRODUCTION DATABASE — e.g. for a deliberate, read-only diagnostic
# session. Never use this to "test changes against prod" — anything this
# container writes, writes to the real production database.
# ============================================================================
#
# Usage: docker compose --env-file deploy/prod.env up --build
# (deploy/docker-compose.yml's own defaults are dev/safe — this file must
# be passed explicitly; there is no accidental way to end up here.)
DB_HOST=192.168.0.162
DB_PORT=6432
BASE_URL=https://api.procurement.cogniwatt.com
